  "details": "Add a animation parameter that allows users to adjust their floor position. This feature would be useful for offsetting toggles related to various footwear options, such as heels or bare feet, and could also enable more creative solutions. Without this parameter, users may experience issues like clipping or floating above the floor when toggling these parts.\n\nI first considered this functionality a long time ago, wondering, \"Why isn't this possible?\" Recently, I was reminded of it when a creator on Booth aimed to develop content for a broader audience, including not only full-body tracking (FBT) users but also half-body and desktop users. They expressed frustration at having to resort to less-than-ideal solutions due to the lack of this functionality.\n\nI'm open to discussing alternative solutions beyond just an animation parameter. Perhaps a component similar to a VRC parameter driver, or another approach, might be more suitable for this purpose. I’m interested in exploring different options that could effectively address the need for adjusting floor positions in various contexts.\n\nI’m not sure if any Asians will read this, but regardless, I’ll post the first paragraph in each language. ChatGPT\n\n사용자가 바닥 위치를 조정할 수 있는 파라미터를 추가하세요. 이 기능은 힐이나 맨발 같은 다양한 신발 옵션과 관련된 토글을 조정하는 데 유용하며, 더 창의적인 해결책을 제공할 수도 있습니다. 이 파라미터가 없으면, 사용자는 이러한 부품을 토글할 때 클리핑이나 바닥 위에 떠 있는 문제를 겪을 수 있습니다.\n\nユーザーが床の位置を調整できるパラメータを追加してください。この機能は、ヒールや裸足などのさまざまな靴のオプションに関連するトグルを補正するのに役立ち、より創造的な解決策も可能にします。このパラメータがないと、ユーザーはこれらのパーツをトグルする際にクリッピングや床から浮く問題が発生する可能性があります。\n\n添加一个允许用户调整地板位置的参数。这个功能对于调整与各种鞋类选项（如高跟鞋或赤脚）相关的切换非常有用，并且还可以启用更具创意的解决方案。如果没有这个参数，用户在切换这些部件时可能会遇到如穿模或浮在地面上等问题。",
